{"term":"aim","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1c9506076fdf6a6b7d","definition":"The pointing of a weapon, as a gun, a dart, or an arrow, or object, in the line of direction with the object intended to be struck; the line of fire; the direction of anything, such as a spear, a blow, a discourse, a remark, towards a particular point or object, with a view to strike or affect it.","example":"to take aim","pos":"noun","synonyms":["design","end","ettle","intention","mint","object","purpose","scheme","scope","tendency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aim assist","aimbot","aim community","aim-crier","aimful","aimless","aimpoint","aimworthy","cry aim","take aim"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b452cde9904ff8f0ce","definition":"The level of accuracy of a weapon.","example":"A rifle has more precise aim than a shotgun.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["design","end","ettle","intention","mint","object","purpose","scheme","scope","tendency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aim assist","aimbot","aim community","aim-crier","aimful","aimless","aimpoint","aimworthy","cry aim","take aim"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0cfccaf6cbdccac62a","definition":"The point intended to be hit, or object intended to be attained or affected.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["design","end","ettle","intention","mint","object","purpose","scheme","scope","tendency"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aim assist","aimbot","aim community","aim-crier","aimful","aimless","aimpoint","aimworthy","cry aim","take aim"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wikt